  "question": {
    "text": "If the pair of straight lines $x^2-2 p x y-y^2=0$ and $x^2-2 p x y-y^2=0$ be such that each pair bisects the angle between the other pair, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ocGVq",
      "text": "\n$p q=-1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gsidF",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{p}=\\mathrm{q}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "iywam",
      "text": "\n$p=-q$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "b5teH",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{pq}=1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of bisector of both pair of straight lines,\n$p x^2+2 x y-p y^2=0$      <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/GY7k7CsxrvaNzWMnf8_JnT8br2MD-jygIk4krkFptj4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$q x^2+2 x y-q y^2=0$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9UXNq1bO9o5PNsIBqAmiW3wIT2KHkRmuKqEkARwFxsg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nFrom (1) and (2).     $\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{1}=\\frac{2}{-2 \\mathrm{p}}=\\frac{-\\mathrm{q}}{-1} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{pq}=-1$",
    "image": null
  },
